From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OpenSession: send the open session id whole

Response parameter sizes are in bytes; SESSION_ALREADY_OPEN gave 1, so
the response carried one byte of the session id (13 bytes, not 16), and
libmtp then failed to open a device whose earlier client left without
CloseSession.
---
diff --git a/src/mtp_operations/mtp_op_opensession.c b/src/mtp_operations/mtp_op_opensession.c
--- a/src/mtp_operations/mtp_op_opensession.c
+++ b/src/mtp_operations/mtp_op_opensession.c
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ uint32_t mtp_op_OpenSession(mtp_ctx * ctx,MTP_PACKET_HEADER * mtp_packet_hdr, i
 	if(ctx->fs_db)
 	{
 		ret_params[0] = ctx->session_id;
-		*ret_params_size = 1;
+		*ret_params_size = sizeof(uint32_t);
 		return MTP_RESPONSE_SESSION_ALREADY_OPEN;
 	}
 
